.git
.claude
.gitignore
.env
.venv
.venv311
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
docs/
eval/
*.md
!requirements.txt
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
codebase/frontend/node_modules
data/
# Except the RAG source corpus (sources.csv + raw/*.md) — scripts/
# docker-entrypoint.sh runs the ingestion pipeline (codebase/models/rag/
# ingest.py) against these on every container boot, writing into the
# Chroma collection at chroma_persist_dir (a mounted Railway volume in
# production, so it survives redeploys — see that volume's own notes).
# Without these files in the image, ingestion has nothing to embed and
# every chat QA question silently "finds nothing" even though the code and
# DB are otherwise fine — this exact failure mode shipped to production
# once already when data/chroma/ was baked in but the corpus files weren't,
# and a stale/empty bake could silently shadow the volume anyway (whichever
# is mounted at the same path wins), which is why the persisted Chroma
# store itself is no longer baked into the image at all.
!data/knowledge_base/sources.csv
!data/knowledge_base/raw/
!data/knowledge_base/raw/**
